---
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";

const sections = [
  ["local-data", "Data stored locally"],
  ["outbound-data", "Data sent to other services"],
  ["controls", "Your controls"],
  ["retention", "Retention"],
  ["contact", "Contact"],
] as const;
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy - Akeru Bot"
  description="How Akeru Bot stores local data and sends data to services you choose."
  heading="Akeru Bot Privacy Policy"
  lede="Akeru Bot is local-first software. This draft explains what stays on your device and what leaves it when you use an online feature."
  status="Draft - counsel review required"
  lastUpdated="2026-08-31"
  sections={sections}
>
  <section id="local-data">
    <p class="section-number">01</p>
    <h2>Data stored locally</h2>
    <p>
      Akeru Bot stores projects, threads, settings, secrets, logs, reviewed policy versions, and
      cached data under the Akeru Bot data directory on the environment you control. The project
      does not require a hosted Akeru account. Direct remote connections may carry this data between
      your own devices and environment.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="outbound-data">
    <p class="section-number">02</p>
    <h2>Data sent to other services</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Agent providers.</strong> Prompts, selected files, tool results, screenshots, and
        conversation context go to the provider CLI or service you choose. That provider controls
        its own processing and retention.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Product feedback.</strong> Feedback you submit goes to feedback.akeru.bot and may be
        kept for up to 90 days.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Voice.</strong> During a voice call, microphone audio and session data go to the
        ChatGPT Realtime service.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Updates.</strong> Provider checks contact provider release sources. Signed desktop
        builds contact the configured release host to check for and download updates.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Optional analytics.</strong> If you opt in and the distributor configures PostHog,
        Akeru Bot sends app version, platform, architecture, client type, and feature events with a
        random installation identifier. It does not use a provider account identifier.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="controls">
    <p class="section-number">03</p>
    <h2>Your controls</h2>
    <p>
      Privacy settings let you turn analytics, product feedback, voice calls, and provider update
      checks on or off. Analytics starts off. You can stop provider data transfers by not starting
      a provider run or by disconnecting that provider.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="retention">
    <p class="section-number">04</p>
    <h2>Retention</h2>
    <p>
      Local data remains until you remove it. Akeru Bot does not control the retention rules of your
      selected providers, release hosts, app stores, or ChatGPT. Review those services before you
      send confidential or regulated data.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <p class="section-number">05</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Report privacy questions through the Akeru Bot repository. This draft must receive qualified
      legal counsel review before any public release.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
